From: shuuri-labs <61762328+shuuri-labs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:27:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mobiletaskswitcher: only the swiped screen's view acts on a
 gesture

With two screens the task switcher gesture breaks: the switcher closes as
soon as the finger lifts, and the other screen's apps get minimized.

The effect creates one view per screen, but the gesture state is shared
and the touch border callback drops the output the swipe started on. Every
view follows the touch and handles the release: a view whose screen has no
tasks calls close(), whose animation ends in instantHide() and deactivates
the switcher on every screen, and each view minimizes its own screen's
windows on activation.

The touch border now reports the output a gesture starts on, the state
exposes it as gestureScreen, and the other screens' views stay passive for
that gesture: hidden, not minimizing, not touching the shared state. A
swipe while the switcher is already open keeps the screen it opened on.
Opening the switcher without a gesture clears it, so the shortcut still
opens it on every screen.

Drop when upstream mobiletaskswitcher tracks the gesture's output; not
filed upstream yet.
